WEBVTT

00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:16,190
When I'm supposed to be dairy-free, can I still eat raw dairy? And the answer is,

00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:23,310
no, you can't. So this is a question from somebody who has cancer, right? And if dairy is driving

00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:29,710
your cancer, then it doesn't make a difference if it's pasteurized, if it's homogenized, if it's

00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:36,990
not pasteurized and homogenized. It doesn't also make a difference whether it's cow dairy or

00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:46,190
goat dairy or sheep dairy. So all of those have the capability of driving cancer

00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:53,550
and stimulating growth of cancer. So we tested you to be dairy-free, we test all those

00:00:53,550 --> 00:01:00,670
dairy. So now this is different. This would be a different question if the person was asking

00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:05,310
because they don't have cancer and it's not because the dairy is driving the cancer.

00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:13,790
But if they have a dairy allergy, so if the person did, let's say, food sensitivity test,

00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:21,630
let's say they did a Cyrix array for testing for cross-reactions to gluten or array 10.

00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:28,990
These are testing for KC and the reason why I like the Cyrix is it does differentiate between

00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:37,550
different types of dairy. Add it differentiates the form of dairy, meaning it might be cow's milk

00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:45,150
is positive, but cheese you can eat. So some people that have a KC sensitivity that's a totally

00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:52,190
different ball of wax and they may not react to a certain type of cheese, but they react to

00:01:52,990 --> 00:02:02,110
another type of cheese or they react to milk itself. For instance, I know people who could

00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:07,790
eat goats, cheese, we're talking about cancer patients who are talking about people with a sensitivity

00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:14,270
and can eat goats, cheese, but they can't eat cow's cheese. It's because the KC is slightly changed

00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:20,750
and differentiated and the protein itself is different between sources and the protein can be

00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:27,950
different and changed and altered when in the cooking process, but that has to do with sensitivity,

00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:36,590
that has to do with the presence of antibodies to a protein or a peptide or should have a protein.

00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:43,150
So when we talk about cancer and what's driving the cancer, I recommend the dairy free. It doesn't make

00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:47,150
any difference in raw dairy, it doesn't make any difference what type of dairy means sheep's dairy,

00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:55,230
goat's dairy, cow's dairy. And it's like caveat to those who sometimes ask this question,

00:02:55,790 --> 00:03:00,990
are eggs dairy, don't you talk about dairy is coming out of a butter about an animal. So

00:03:02,270 --> 00:03:04,270
don't believe it, there's nothing.

